# Sustainable Fashion Research Plan Revision Update<br>
<br>
## Abstract<br>
This plan outlines a comprehensive approach to sustainable fashion, focusing on reducing waste and promoting eco-friendly practices in the fashion industry. The research will involve conducting interviews with key stakeholders, analyzing existing literature, and developing a framework for implementing sustainable fashion practices.<br>
<br>
## Methodology<br>
The study will employ a mixed-methods approach, combining both qualitative and quantitative data collection methods. This includes:<br>
<br>
* Conducting semi-structured interviews with fashion designers, manufacturers, and retailers to gather insights on current challenges and opportunities in sustainable fashion.<br>
* Analyzing existing literature on sustainable fashion, including academic papers, industry reports, and government publications.<br>
* Developing a framework for implementing sustainable fashion practices, incorporating best practices from the literature review and interview findings.<br>
<br>
## Expected Outcomes<br>
The study aims to:<br>
<br>
* Identify key drivers of sustainable fashion adoption among fashion designers, manufacturers, and retailers.<br>
* Develop a comprehensive framework for implementing sustainable fashion practices in the industry.<br>
* Provide recommendations for policymakers, industry leaders, and consumers on how to promote sustainable fashion.<br>
<br>
## Timeline<br>
The research will be conducted over the next three months, with regular progress updates and milestones. The final report will be submitted within six weeks of project completion.<br>
<br>
